    "economics_flip": "Measured on clud: a main-push run is 14.9 runner-min, 7.1 (48%) skippable. At 1.63 pushes/day reuse saves ~5 runner-min/day, while a nightly minimal-tier run costs 14.9/day and a full-tier one ~60/day. The design's drift backstop costs 3-12x what it protects at clud's real push rate (the design assumed ~30 pushes/day). Prefer --max-age-hours over a nightly until a repo's push rate justifies one.",
